            <ArticleTitle>[Value of esophageal manometry with the methylergometrin maleate test in angina with normal coronarography. The concept of esophageal angina].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>22 patients presenting an &quot;angina with normal coronarography&quot; and 5 control subjects were subjected to a manometric exploration of the oesophagus in the basal state and under methylergometrine maleate (MEM) treatment. The MEM test is shown to be a good one for the induction of painful oesophageal dyskinesias, particularly in patients who had suffered in an inexplicable manner when that substance was administered for coronarography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
